      "latin": "probātor, probātōris m.",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "late",
      "gloss": "an examiner, one who tries or tests",
      "evidence": [
        "Vulg. Jer. 20.12 (Lewis &amp; Short: “a trier, examiner”)"
      ],
      "comment": "Classically an approver (Cic., Ov.); a trier or examiner in the Vulgate (Lewis &amp; Short). That is the sense here; its application to one who tests software is ours. Traupman and Morgan–Owens have no word for a tester."
    },
